    "member_id": "platform-options-forwarding-gaps-20261014"
  },
  "context": "These are follow-ups from #2972 (platform options reach adapters) and #2974 (deployment modes). Extend the per-platform parity test from #2972 to these platforms. If the shape of recorded `platform_options` changes, it touches results identity: published `result_id`s must not change, so check against the corpus first.\n\n2026-10-17: SQLite `database_name` is now applied (#3048, 7959be931), but `tests/unit/cli/test_platform_options_reach_adapters.py` still lists it in `KNOWN_UNAPPLIED_OPTIONS`; remove that entry. The plan-option exemption (`plan_max_depth`, `plan_capture_timeout_seconds`) on the hand-written `from_config` platforms is the main remaining gap; shrink it as each platform forwards the options. Owner, 2026-10-15, Claude session e0e74e6b, question dialog: \"Keep follow-up tracker items\".",
  "description": "These options are accepted but never reach the adapter:\n- The hand-written `from_config` methods of emr-serverless, dataproc, dataproc-serverless, synapse-spark, fabric-spark and snowpark-connect do not forward `plan_max_depth` or `plan_capture_timeout_seconds`.\n- SQLite parses `database_name` but never reads it.\n- TimescaleDB `from_config` drops `service_url`.\n- glue and dataproc-serverless register no platform options at all.\n\nSeparately, supplied options are lifted only in `get_platform_config`, not in the default builder. The default builder was left alone because `DatabaseConfig` has `extra=\"allow\"`, so lifting there would change the recorded `platform_options` shape.",
  "links": [
    "https://github.com/BenchBox-dev/benchbox/pull/2972",
    "https://github.com/BenchBox-dev/benchbox/pull/2974"
  ],
